course: dictionary
lesson: 12572
title: Dilution: making things weaker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dilution is a noun. It comes from the verb «dilute», which means to make a liquid weaker or thinner by adding water or another liquid. The squash is strong, so you add water to make it weaker and easier to drink.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The label says one part squash to ten parts water.» The numbers and the word water tell you that the squash is being made weaker. Try the swap: "the squash was made weaker by adding water" still makes sense, so dilution fits.
explain: Dilution can also mean a weaker form of something that is not a drink. «The dilution of his power after the vote made the leader less feared.» Here the word means weakening, not water. Always check which sense fits the sentence around it.
fact: Dilution means the act of making a liquid weaker or thinner by adding water or another liquid.
fact: «Dilute» is the verb and «dilution» is the noun.
fact: A dilution can also mean the liquid that has been made weaker this way.
fact: In science, dilution means adding solvent so that a solution is less concentrated.
fact: Labels on bleach and cleaning products give the right dilution, so always read them carefully.
exercise: «One part squash to ten parts water» tells you the squash is strong. What does this show about the dilution? | It is made stronger by adding sugar | It is frozen into ice | *It is made weaker by adding water | It is heated until it boils
exercise: «The dilution of the squash was too weak, so the drink tasted of nothing.» What does dilution mean here? | The act of making the squash hotter | *The act of making the squash weaker by adding water | The act of stirring sugar into the squash | The act of pouring the squash into a bottle
exercise: Mum says, «Dilute the bleach before you clean the sink.» Which word is the verb form of dilution? | sink | clean | *dilute | bleach
test: «The label gave the dilution for the cleaner: one part cleaner to four parts water.» What is the dilution for the cleaner? | Four parts cleaner to one part water | Only cleaner, with no water at all | Water heated to boiling | *One part cleaner to four parts water
test: «The dilution of his power after the vote made the leader less feared.» What does dilution mean in this sentence? | A strong new power | A sudden rise in his fame | A liquid for cleaning windows | *The weakening of his power
exam: «The scientist made a dilution by adding 90 millilitres of water to 10 millilitres of juice, so the juice became weaker.» What does dilution mean here? | A test to find out who is the best scientist | A cup used for measuring | A strong juice with no water | *A liquid made weaker by adding water
